icipants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/111376"} "45 from 19 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "West Germany had shown a considerable depth of talent since the 1984 Olympics and had taken 5 of the 9 available medals at the intervening World Championships – each by a different fencer. It was expected that the West Germans would all be strong medal contenders but the extent of their domination came as a shock. There was little sign of German superiority in the second pool stages as all three had difficulty qualifying but once in the knockout stages they suddenly found their best form. " [:a {:href "/athletes/20700"} "Anja Fichtel"] "’s victory over " [:a {:href "/athletes/20740"} "Zsuzsa Jánosi"] " of Hungary in the semi-final ensured that the West Germans would take home both gold and silver and with Jánosi losing to " [:a {:href "/athletes/20701"} "Zita-Eva Funkenhauser"] " in the bronze medal match the medal sweep was complete. This just left the matter of which German would be crowned Olympic champion. That honour fell to Fichtel who defeated " [:a {:href "/athletes/102622"} "Sabine Bau"] " to add Olympic gold to her 1986 World title."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Back in 29th place in the classification was 52 year old " [:a {:href "/athletes/20949"} "Kerstin Palm"] " of Sweden making her 7th successive Olympic appearance. Although since beaten, it was a record for any female Olympian at the time."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "18"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/20700"} "Anja Fichtel"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRG.png"}] "FRG"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"